The above tool calls will output the following information:

* System logs (e.g. Windows Event Logs, Linux Syslog) on the target host 10.0.0.50 for login attempts and process execution.
* Output of the vulnerability scanner that triggered the alert to determine if it was a false positive.
* Network packet capture (PCAP) of the login attempt to confirm the impossible travel time.
* Detailed process execution logs (e.g. Windows Process Monitor, Linux strace) to determine if the exploit payload executed successfully.

Note: The `check_server_logs` function will be called multiple times to retrieve different types of logs. The `verify_network_traffic` function will be called once to verify if malicious outbound beaconing or exploitation has ceased.
